a) $\frac{1}{\sin x} + \frac{1}{\sin \left(x - \frac{3\pi}{2}\right)} = 4\sin \left(\frac{7\pi}{4} - x\right)$;
b) $2\sin x(1 + \cos 2x) + \sin 2x = 1 + 2\cos x;$
c) $\sin^3 x - \sqrt{3} \cos^3 x = \sin x \cos^2 x - \sqrt{3} \sin^2 x \cos x$.

a) $\left(1 + \sin^2 x\right)\cos x + \left(1 + \cos^2 x\right)\sin x = 1 + \sin 2x;$
b) $2\sin^2 2x + \sin 7x - 1 = \sin x$;
c) $\left(\sin \frac{x}{2} + \cos \frac{x}{2}\right)^{2} + \sqrt{3} \cos x = 2.$
